Package: scotty
Architecture: any
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 avahi-daemon,
 bluez,
 libnss-mdns,
 network-manager,
 qml6-module-qtquick,
 qml6-module-qtquick-controls,
 qml6-module-qtquick-dialogs,
 qml6-module-qtquick-effects,
 qml6-module-qtquick-layouts,
 qml6-module-qtquick-window
Recommends:
 gnome-shell-extension-scotty,
 scotty-bluez-compat (= ${binary:Version})
Description: local file sharing with nearby devices
 Scotty sends and receives files directly between Linux, Android, and Windows
 devices using the Nearby/Quick Share protocol. Transfers use the local network,
 an on-demand Wi-Fi hotspot, or Bluetooth without uploading files to a cloud.
 .
 This package contains the application and sharing engine. GNOME Shell and
 system-level BlueZ integration are packaged separately.

Package: gnome-shell-extension-scotty
Architecture: all
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 gnome-shell (>= 46),
 gnome-shell (<< 51),
 scotty (= ${binary:Version})
Description: GNOME Quick Settings integration for Scotty
 Adds a Scotty tile to GNOME Quick Settings. The tile displays visibility and
 transfer state, opens the application through D-Bus activation, and provides
 an explicit Quit action.

Package: scotty-bluez-compat
Architecture: all
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 bluez,
 iw,
 polkitd | policykit-1,
 systemd
Description: system integration required by Scotty transports
 Installs package-owned systemd and Polkit integration for Scotty's Bluetooth
 and on-demand Wi-Fi hotspot transports. It enables BlueZ experimental APIs,
 disables the conflicting MCP plugin, and grants active local users permission
 to manage only Scotty's temporary hotspot-interface unit.
